### QA (qa main 6f8ffcc81f645c6de996a393e8d8015325f85974, `report-build1.md`, `listening.md`, answered `qa`#3)

R1-R9 pass over HTTP (49 clicks = 49 points = 49 sounds, empty/duplicate clicks 0, max up 887 ms, HUD/end/replay correct, mobile viewport + touch OK).
R10 `listening.md`: request and verbatim answers kept. The resource heard a short percussive hit ("kick drum / thump"; "hollow percussive bonk" when asked) and gave 0.5-0.6 s / 0.9 s; QA's controls (0.25 s tone -> 1.1 s, 1.0 s -> 1.37 s) show the resource overestimates sub-second lengths, and measurement gives 0.25 s / 44100 Hz, peak 0.90, no clipping. I accept that as a match: kind matches by the listening, length and rate by measurement.
R9 generator: I confirmed `tools/make_hit.py` in artist 18f595a (numpy, pitch-falling decaying thump, writes sound/hit.wav 0.25 s 44.1 kHz).
Defect `game-developer`#4: opened from file://, fetch of sound/hit.wav fails and no hit sound ever plays. QA rated it minor (README says serve over HTTP); I judge it blocks acceptance, since a user receiving a small web game will commonly double-click index.html and R4 then fails. Revise decision sent there.

